  "ending": {
    "label": "共谋",
    "subtitle": "我握着证据，等天亮，等火烧起来。",
    "passage": "The service door clicks shut behind you, sealing away the gala's golden noise. The alley is a tunnel of cold concrete and the distant wail of a siren, but Elena's hand is warm in yours. You don't look back. You've left Arthur in the ballroom, his laughter still ringing false, his threats still hanging in the air. But out here, under the sodium-orange streetlights, the city feels enormous and indifferent—and for the first time in hours, you can breathe.\n\nIn your apartment, the curtains drawn against the night, you and Elena sit on the floor with the burner phone between you. The texts glow like embers, each one a match that could set Arthur's empire ablaze. She reads them again, her finger tracing the screen, her face a study in fear and resolve. 'We can't just sit on this,' she whispers. 'He'll come for us.'\n\nYou know she's right. Arthur Sterling doesn't lose. He waits, he watches, and he strikes when you least expect it. But tonight, you have something he doesn't: the truth, and the will to use it.\n\nYou draft the message to the journalist from the Daily Ledger—the one who was already sniffing around. You don't send it. Not yet. You save it as a draft, a loaded gun on the nightstand. Then you lean back against the couch, Elena's head on your shoulder, the city's hum a lullaby of distant traffic. The award sits in her bag, tarnished by the lie, but yours now. Not as a trophy, but as a weapon.\n\nTomorrow, the narrative will be yours. Tonight, you are not Arthur's fixer. You are not the keeper of his secrets. You are the one who holds the match, and the whole house of cards is waiting to burn.",
    "tier": "compromised",
    "early_terminated": false,
    "failure_trigger": null,
    "highlights": [
      {
        "beat_ord": 2,
        "headline": "You refuse the rigging and con",
        "body_excerpt": "You step toward Arthur, your voice low but sharp. \"The rigging stops now. We're not going through with this.\" Arthur's jaw tightens; he glances over his shoulder at the stage, where Marcus is now holding the sealed envelope, the live audience's applause swelling.",
        "why_pivotal": "Your first open defiance shifts the power dynamic, revealing your leverage over Arthur and setting the stage for the escalating conflict."
      },
      {
        "beat_ord": 6,
        "headline": "You reveal the burner phone",
        "body_excerpt": "You pull out the burner phone, thumb hovering over the screen. Arthur's eyes drop to it, his smirk faltering. \"You wouldn't,\" he says, but his voice cracks, and you know you've hit something.",
        "why_pivotal": "You brandish your key asset—the incriminating texts—turning the tables and exposing Arthur's vulnerability."
      },
      {
        "beat_ord": 14,
        "headline": "Elena joins your side",
        "body_excerpt": "You pull Elena deeper into the shadows behind the curtain, your voice a whisper. \"We find something on Arthur. Something he can't bury. Then we're not his puppets anymore.\" Elena stares at you, her eyes wide with a mix of fear and a spark of desperate hope.",
        "why_pivotal": "Elena shifts from wary to aligned, becoming your ally and strengthening your position against Arthur."
      },
      {
        "beat_ord": 18,
        "headline": "United front against Arthur",
        "body_excerpt": "You step out of the shadows, Elena at your side, and Arthur's eyes narrow as you approach. \"What's this? A mutiny?\" His voice is a cold blade, but you see the flicker of unease behind his bravado.",
        "why_pivotal": "You and Elena confront Arthur together, solidifying your alliance and delivering a direct challenge to his control."
      },
      {
        "beat_ord": 20,
        "headline": "You threaten to expose everyth",
        "body_excerpt": "You step forward, the phone raised like a shield, the screen's glow casting your face in cold blue. 'Back off, Arthur. I have everything—the texts, the payment trails, the names. One tap and it's over.'",
        "why_pivotal": "You escalate to an ultimatum, leveraging your full inventory to force Arthur's retreat and secure your freedom."
      }
    ],
